# Force LF line endings for shell scripts regardless of the checking-out
# machine's core.autocrlf setting. A CRLF line ending inside `set -euo
# pipefail` (or any bash control-flow line) breaks parsing outright —
# confirmed as a real failure mode (see the git log around the
# test_dispatch_worktree.py fixture fix). Deliberately narrow: Python,
# JS, and Markdown all tolerate either line ending fine, so only files a
# shell interpreter directly executes are pinned here.
*.sh text eol=lf
